  "body_html": "<h1>Binary Knapsack Allocations</h1>\n<p>The binary-allocation layer represents selected agents by Boolean profiles,\nconverts them into real allocation vectors, and defines finite feasible\nknapsack search spaces with a social-welfare objective.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[AGT, Chapter 12, Section 12.2] Nisan, Roughgarden, Tardos, and Vazirani,\n  <em>Algorithmic Game Theory</em>, <code>references/AlgorithmicGameTheory.pdf</code>.\n  Binary allocation rules in single-parameter mechanism-design domains.</li>\n<li>[AGT, Chapter 11, Section 11.2] Nisan, Roughgarden, Tardos, and Vazirani,\n  <em>Algorithmic Game Theory</em>, <code>references/AlgorithmicGameTheory.pdf</code>.\n  Single-minded combinatorial-auction feasibility and welfare objectives.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Provenance</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Migrated from EconCSLib pull request 27, old blueprint label\n  <code>def:auction_knapsack_binary</code> in <code>blueprint/src/content.tex</code>.</li>\n</ul>",
